# Upstream progress watches. Nothing consumes these values -- Renovate does:
# each line pins the current state of an upstream issue or PR through the
# custom.github-state datasource (renovate.json5), 0 = open, 1 = closed.
# When it closes upstream, Renovate opens a PR bumping the line -- that PR
# is the notification; merging it is only an acknowledgement.
#
# c/image support for cosign v3's Sigstore bundle format. While this is
# open, both our signatures (keyed and keyless) must stay on
# --new-bundle-format=false in build.yml. PR #567 for it was closed
# unmerged.
# renovate: datasource=custom.github-state depName=podman-container-tools/container-libs/issues/388
CONTAINER_LIBS_ISSUE_388_CLOSED=0
#
# Fulcio workflow-identity (URI) verification for containers-policy.json --
# the gate on enforcing our keyless signatures on-device (policy matches
# Fulcio by subjectEmail only today; see container-libs#34). When this
# merges and reaches bootc/rpm-ostree, the on-device switch to keyless
# becomes a policy change.
# renovate: datasource=custom.github-state depName=podman-container-tools/container-libs/pulls/625
CONTAINER_LIBS_PR_625_CLOSED=0
#
# The durable issue behind PR#625 above: policy.json matching Fulcio
# identities by subjectEmail only. Watched separately because the PR could
# close unmerged; the issue closing means the capability is real.
# renovate: datasource=custom.github-state depName=podman-container-tools/container-libs/issues/34
CONTAINER_LIBS_ISSUE_34_CLOSED=0
#
# The consumer-side twin of issue #388: rpm-ostree failing to verify the
# new bundle format. Both closing is the end-to-end signal that the
# on-device stack reads cosign v3's default format.
# renovate: datasource=custom.github-state depName=coreos/rpm-ostree/issues/5509
RPM_OSTREE_ISSUE_5509_CLOSED=0
